{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"5fd1774a69ed9fbaf963d9c9f464b9c17fa63059e1950d62a4d5002857bc702b","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan-review sidecar recall mechanism","key_entities":["sidecar.prior_concerns","pass1.run_pass1","build_payload._slim","review_kernel/verify.finding_listing","review_kernel/decide.py","attest.current_material_fingerprint","material_fingerprint","evidence","impact","_recall marker","norm_id n9d22a867f4a4d027"],"problem_keywords":["plan-review finding replay","recall ratchet","re-grounding","empty evidence","material fingerprint","pass-2 verification"],"propositions":["Prior plan-review findings with empty evidence are recalled verbatim on every subsequent review even after the plan is edited to address them, causing a self-feeding ratchet instead of convergence.","The recall injection hardcodes evidence to empty list, so Pass-2 verification cannot re-ground the finding against the current plan text and rubber-stamps the bare assertion instead.","A prior finding with no persisted grounding evidence should be ineligible for recall, breaking the ratchet and working retroactively on already-written sidecars.","Recall should be suppressed when the prior sidecar's material_fingerprint differs from the current material_fingerprint, since finder silence on changed material indicates the edit resolved the finding."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787317399866901001,"uuid":"d3edeb51-fd64-4d8a-9481-bc63a68e04ca"}